xv6-rpi4
xv6-rpi4 has been confirmed on an actual Raspberry Pi 4B.
NOT implemented: micro sd driver
BUILD:
  - run on raspberry pi 4B:
    1. modify `SDPATH` in Makefile to your sd card's directory
    2. `make rpi4` will generate kernel8.img and copy to `SDPATH`
    (claude: upstream also had a step 1 here, "delete `ASFLAGS +=
     -DRPI4_QEMU` in Makefile" - no longer needed, and the flag is gone.
     kernel/entry.S reads CurrentEL at runtime to tell a QEMU boot (EL3)
     from a real-firmware one (EL2), so the same kernel8.img is correct
     on both. See that file's comment on _entry.)
  - run on qemu
    1. `make qemu`, with a mainline qemu >= 9.1 on PATH - 9.1 is the
       first release with a Raspberry Pi 4 board at all (`-M raspi4b`,
       the default here now). Boots to a shell and passes usertests;
       verified on 11.1.50. This repo's top-level `make run-arm64-pi4` /
       `make test-arm64-pi4` do it with the qemu ./configure found.
    2. or, for the qemu fork this port was originally developed against,
       clone and build qemu-patch-raspberry4
       (https://github.com/k-mrm/qemu-patch-raspberry4), then
       `make qemu QEMUPREFIX=<path>/qemu-patch-raspberry4/build/
       QEMUMACHINE=raspi4b1g QEMUMEM=1G`

Serial Communication:
  xv6-rpi4 use uart0
  baudrate: 115200

